 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage: TodoMVC build — Specs and watchbill authored
+## Voyage: DOM identity — Specs strengthened
 
-Spec source: `assets/app-spec.md`
-Template source: `assets/app-template.index.html`
-Implementation: Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence.
-Verification tier: happy-dom (already rigged — world.js exists, tier default @logic).
+An external Cypress acceptance suite reports "element detached from DOM" errors on:
+- Mark all as completed
+- Clear complete state of all items
+- Mark items as complete
+- Un-mark items as complete
+- Save edits on blur
 
-### Specs authored covering all app-spec.md behaviours
+Root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` removes ALL existing `<li>` elements from the DOM
+(unconditional for-in loop with removeChild), then recreates them.  The existing conformance
+scenarios only checked for `innerHTML` text in source (passing), missing this removeChild-based
+rebuild.  New scenarios detect the real pattern.
 
-- `features/todo-management.feature` — new todo, no-todos visibility, counter, whitespace trim, empty guard
-- `features/todo-completion.feature` — toggle single, mark all, clear completed, toggle-all sync
-- `features/todo-editing.feature` — double-click edit, save on Enter/blur, cancel on Escape, empty destroys
-- `features/routing.feature` — #/, #/active, #/completed routes, selected class, live filter on state change
-- `features/persistence.feature` — localStorage save/restore, completion persistence, no editing state persisted
+### Changes
 
-### watchbill.json
+- `features/conformance/dom-identity.feature` — 2 new scenarios:
+  1. Source check: detects unconditionial removeChild loop + createElement after (RED)
+  2. Runtime check: captures li element references, toggles all, asserts same nodes remain (RED)
+- `features/support/conformance-steps.js` — step definitions for the new scenarios
+- `watchbill.json` — 2 targets pointing at the failing scenarios
 
-24 scenario targets across 5 watches. Ordered: display -> completion -> editing -> routing -> persistence.
+The 2 new scenarios FAIL on current code.  All 26 existing scenarios still PASS.
 
-### Next
