 Feature: DOM identity preservation
 
-  When the todo list state changes (toggle, add, remove, edit) the render
-  function MUST mutate existing DOM nodes in place — toggle classes, set
-  .checked, update textContent — rather than rebuilding the list from
-  scratch via innerHTML. Rebuilding destroys every existing <li> node,
-  which detaches any browser-held reference and causes Cypress
-  acceptance tests to fail with "element detached from DOM".
+  When the todo list state changes (toggle, add, remove, edit) every
+  existing <li> element MUST be mutated in place (toggle classes, set
+  .checked, update textContent) rather than removed from the DOM and
+  recreated.  Removing and recreating elements destroys every existing
+  <li> node, which invalidates browser-held references and causes
+  Cypress acceptance tests to fail with "element detached from DOM".
 
-  The fix: replace `todoList.innerHTML = html` with a diff loop that
-  reuses existing <li> elements.
+  The render function's stale-node removal loop currently iterates ALL
+  existing items and calls removeChild on every one, then creates new
+  nodes for the full filtered list — equivalent to an innerHTML rebuild
+  without using innerHTML.  Fix: the stale-removal loop MUST test
+  membership in the filtered list and only remove nodes NOT present.
 
